`resolveDeferredLink` runs **at most once per browser** (it records one install on our side). It never throws: on any error it resolves to `{ matched: false, matchMethod: 'none' }`, so it's safe to await on startup.

From a website, send events with your publishable key. When `resolveDeferredLink` matched, its result also has `clickId`, the tap this visit came from; send it with the event so the revenue lands on that tap. The web SDK doesn't remember it for you, so keep it if you send events later.

```ts
await fetch('https://strait.link/v1/event', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    publishableKey: 'st_pub_live_…',
    event: 'purchase',
    value: 49.99,
    currency: 'USD',
    clickId: result.clickId,     // the matched tap, if any
  }),
});
```

