### In the dashboard

Open **Dashboard → Import → From Branch**, choose the export file and select **Preview**. Each row shows the slug, the destination and the path your app will get, the fallbacks, the social preview, the campaign and tags, and any problems. Select **Import**. You get a summary of what was created and what wasn't (with the reason), and you can download the rows that failed as a CSV, fix them and import them again with **Bulk create**.

Imports are safe to run twice: a slug that already exists is reported, never overwritten.

### With the API

`POST /v1/links/batch` creates up to 500 links per call with your secret key. Each item takes the same fields as `POST /v1/links` and gets its own result, so one bad item never fails the batch. A slug that already exists (or repeats earlier in the batch) is a `409` for that item only.

```bash
curl https://strait.link/v1/links/batch \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $SECRET_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "links": [
      {
        "slug": "p42",
        "longUrl": "https://shop.example.com/product/42",
        "desktopUrl": "https://shop.example.com/products/42",
        "iosFallbackUrl": "https://shop.example.com/ios/42",
        "androidFallbackUrl": "https://shop.example.com/android/42",
        "title": "Product 42",
        "campaign": "summer_2026",
        "tags": ["sale"]
      },
      { "slug": "summer-sale", "longUrl": "https://shop.example.com/sale/summer?utm_source=instagram" }
    ]
  }'
```

```json
{
  "results": [
    { "index": 0, "ok": true, "status": 201, "link": { "slug": "p42", "shortUrl": "https://<handle>.strait.link/p42", … } },
    { "index": 1, "ok": false, "status": 409, "error": "slug already exists in this workspace" }
  ],
  "summary": { "total": 2, "created": 1, "failed": 1 }
}
```

Each item's `status` is what `POST /v1/links` would have answered: `201`, `400` (invalid, or `destination_blocked`), `402` (plan limit reached) or `409`. See the [REST API](https://straitlink.in/docs/api/#batch-create).

